% Hand-written. The package has no roxygen2 build step — jmvtools regenerates
% R/*.h.R but never touches man/ — so this file is the documentation, not a
% generated artefact. Keep it in step with the roxygen block in R/pgs_weights.R.
\name{pgs_weights}
\alias{pgs_weights}
\title{Read a PGS-Catalog weights file for use with snpPGS}
\usage{
pgs_weights(path)
}
\arguments{
\item{path}{Path to a PGS-Catalog format file (\code{.csv}, \code{.tsv},
\code{.txt} or their \code{.gz} forms).}
}
\value{
A named list with \code{weightsContent} (the file's bytes, base64-encoded) and
\code{weightsFilename}, suitable for splicing into a \code{snpPGS} call.
}
\description{
Reads \code{path} and returns the pair of \code{snpPGS} arguments that
carry a weights file: the base64-encoded file contents and its name.
}
\details{
\code{snpPGS} deliberately has no weights-file \emph{path} option. A jamovi
analysis stores its options inside the \code{.omv} file and re-runs them when
that file is opened, so a stored path would be resolved against the filesystem
of whoever opened it rather than the author's — letting a shared document read
files from a collaborator's machine. Carrying the file's \emph{contents} removes
that entirely, and is also what lets the analysis work unchanged in jamovi
cloud, where the R engine runs on a different machine from the browser.

This helper is the scripting equivalent of the file-browse button in the jamovi
UI: it reads the file once, here, in the caller's own session — the same act as
\code{read.csv()} — and hands back the two arguments that travel with the
analysis.

A \code{.gz} file is passed through still compressed; \code{snpPGS} decompresses
it based on the \code{.gz} extension in the file name. Files larger than 64 MB
are refused, the same ceiling the backend applies after decompression.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
w <- pgs_weights("pgs_catalog.csv")

# splice the pair into the call
do.call(snpPGS, c(list(data = mydata, snpCols = c("rs123", "rs456")), w))

# or pass them explicitly
snpPGS(data = mydata, snpCols = c("rs123", "rs456"),
       weightsContent  = w$weightsContent,
       weightsFilename = w$weightsFilename)
}
}
\seealso{
\code{snpPGS}, whose \code{weightsContent} / \code{weightsFilename} arguments
this fills in. It is generated by the jamovi compiler and carries no \file{.Rd}
page of its own, so it is named here rather than linked.
}
